  "revised": "2026-10-17",
  "source": "Chauvin Arnoux Energy, \"MODBUS interface - ENERIUM 100/200/300 V2\", MS1-7423 Ed06",
  "sources": [{"title": "MODBUS interface - ENERIUM 100/200/300 V2", "version": "MS1-7423 Ed06", "url": "https://www.chauvin-arnoux-energy.com/sites/default/files/HLHBULL5.PDF", "note": "Appendix 3, Modbus addressing"}],
  "notes": [
    "Registers are read with FC03 or FC04 (identical). Settings are changed with command words written with FC16 to the command zone (0xD000), not by writing the setting registers directly.",
    "Data are big-endian, high word first.",
    "RS-485 defaults: 9600 baud, no parity, 1 stop bit, Modbus RTU. The front optical port is fixed at 38400 baud, 8N1.",
    "Each 64-bit energy is a pair of 32-bit counters: the low part in Wh (varh, VAh) and the high part in MWh (Mvarh, MVAh).",
    "Not in this map: alarms, inputs and outputs, minimum, maximum and average values, harmonics, curves, power quality events and waveforms."
  ],
